      "title_align": "left",
      "section": "Pick two groups",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "The collection is a wide matrix: one row per cell, one column per gene. Box-select cells on the scatter and save the selection as a group from the Analysis panel, twice, then pick the two groups on the right and press Compare. The test runs as a background job and its result is cached, so the same comparison comes back instantly. With no saved group the two pickers fall back to the cluster labels the matrix shipped with. Six genes were planted as cluster markers, so a comparison between two clusters should return exactly those four that belong to them.\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/advanced_viz_demo"
    },
